"""Integrate remaining adopted precision edits without adding a second story."""
from pathlib import Path
import json,re
from revise_html_review import replace,paragraph,log
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];OUT=ROOT/'review-revision/html-review-implementation'
def main():
    m=(ROOT/'manuscript/main.tex').read_text();a=(ROOT/'manuscript/appendix.tex').read_text()
    def M(old,new,ids):
        nonlocal m;m=replace(m,old,new,ids,'main.tex')
    def A(old,new,ids):
        nonlocal a;a=replace(a,old,new,ids,'appendix.tex')
    M(r'A stopping certificate uses fixed maps, visible base scores and revealed candidate test scores to verify churn-budget feasibility and a retained-count gap.',r'A stopping certificate uses fixed maps, visible base scores and queried candidate scores to verify churn feasibility and bound count shortfall from the full-information optimum.','E019')
    M('Offline construction chooses entries with knowledge of the true bit matrix. A verifier sees only revealed entries and checks every consistent Boolean completion.', 'An offline constructor uses the true bit matrix to choose entries. The verifier sees only revealed entries and checks every consistent Boolean completion.','E028')
    M(r'Attainment allocates $b+1$ oppositions across the $p$ cheapest true rows, with row $i$ capped at $\min(z_{(i)},t^*)$, and reveals $t^*$ oppositions in every other row.',r'To attain the bound offline, order rows by true cost. Reveal $b+1$ oppositions across the first $p$ rows, capped at $\min(z_{(i)},t^*)$ in row $i$, and $t^*$ oppositions in every remaining row.','E032')
    M(r'Sorting active selected costs solves the mask problem in $O(m\log m)$ time, adding invariant selected rows at zero churn cost.',r'At each update, sorting active selected costs computes a retained-count capacity in $O(m\log m)$ time; invariant selected rows add zero churn cost.','E037')
    M('If exact stopping occurs early, its state is reused at later allowances without further queries.', 'If exact certification precedes a later inspection checkpoint, its state is reused without further queries.','E043')
    M('All-decision cardinality may spend budget on exclusions; selected retention spends it on returned outputs.', 'All-decision cardinality may spend budget on exclusions, which add no returned outputs; selected retention spends it only on baseline-selected outputs.','E047')
    M(r'If its threshold is batch feasible, the best feasible threshold in the same nested family retains at least as many decisions (Appendix~\ref{app:baselines}).',r'When its threshold is test-batch feasible, the best feasible threshold in the same nested family retains at least as many decisions; their guarantees still differ (Appendix~\ref{app:baselines}).','E048')
    M(r'Appendix~\ref{app:review-score} gives costs and the reduction; unequal-size WMT24 documents are excluded.',r'Appendix~\ref{app:review-score} gives the reduction and costs. Unequal-size WMT24 documents are excluded from this equal-size-group comparison.','E050')
    M('Initial row-total Spearman correlation does not determine discovery cost.', 'Higher initial row-total Spearman correlation does not consistently identify the acquisition rule with fewer queries.','E052')
    M('Agreements can dominate when nearly all boundary rows must be retained; oppositions exclude larger sets.', 'Agreement observations can dominate the minimum when nearly all boundary rows must be retained; oppositions certify that no larger set is feasible.','E054')
    M(r'Appendix~\ref{app:granularity} reports tails and zero witnesses.',r'Appendix~\ref{app:granularity} reports ratio tails and separately counts zero offline minima.','E055')
    M('Evidence requirements and discovery order both affect inspection; each minimum concerns its own stopping target.',r'Along a fixed path, changing $\alpha$ changes the safety and exclusion evidence needed for stopping, so inspection need not decrease monotonically.','E056')
    M(r'For thirteen-stream WMT23 median at $q=.05$, pool-wise 40-split mean inspection has median \compWmtMedianActive\% and descriptive 10th--90th percentiles \compWmtMedianLow--\compWmtMedianHigh\%.',r'On thirteen-stream WMT23 median at $q=.05$, first averaging each pool over 40 splits gives 20 pool means with median \compWmtMedianActive\% and descriptive 10th--90th percentiles \compWmtMedianLow--\compWmtMedianHigh\%.','E057')
    M(r'A query-priority tie rule was repaired later after an exact-replay failure (Appendix~\ref{app:review-quality}).',r'After an exact-replay failure, we repaired WMT24 query-priority ties, changing order rather than integer costs or certificate inequalities (Appendix~\ref{app:review-quality}).','E058')
    M('Low median query counts thus coincide with high initial coverage.', 'Low median inspection largely coincides with high initial coverage; it alone does not establish a superior query order.','E060')
    M(r'At $q=.05$, relaxing nominal count tolerance to $.10$ leaves reference priority with mean pooling querying 72.4--76.2\% of active entries across all six panels (Appendix~\ref{app:tolerance}).',r'At $q=.05$, count tolerance $\eta=.10$ still leaves reference-priority mean pooling inspecting 72.4--76.2\% across six panels. This changes $\varepsilon=\lceil\eta|S_0|\rceil$, not $\alpha$ (Appendix~\ref{app:tolerance}).','E061')
    M(r'Both total-count-matched and annotated-count-matched MQM comparisons have differences of either sign and concern observed labels only; masks and paths are fixed before label use, and missing labels stay missing (Appendix~\ref{app:review-quality}).',r'Total-count-matched and annotated-count-matched MQM differences have either sign. Masks and paths stay fixed and missing labels are not imputed; neither comparison estimates unannotated-output quality (Appendix~\ref{app:review-quality}).','E063')
    M(r'Under the original protocol, RewardBench\textquotesingle s primary stop at $q=.05$, $\alpha=.10$ reveals 1.77\% of $NT$ scores through median entry queries versus 71.8\% through columns; mean fractions are 4.52\% and 96.1\%.',r'Under reference priority on RewardBench at $q=.05$, $\alpha=.10$ and the primary positive-gap stop, median entry queries reveal 1.77\% of all $NT$ candidate-test scores versus 71.8\% through columns; mean fractions are 4.52\% and 96.1\%.','E066')
    M(r'Separately, for exact median stopping, minimum column witnesses average \granRbColumns{} columns (\granRbMinimum\%) versus \granRbOnlineColumns{} for reference order;',r'For the separate exact median target, minimum column certificates average \granRbColumns{} columns (\granRbMinimum\% of $NT$ scores) versus \granRbOnlineColumns{} for reference order;','E067')
    M(r'At $m=128,T=12,b=0$ with one opposition per row, every layout needs 128 entry observations.',r'At $m=128,T=12,b=0$ with one opposition per row, the minimum exact entry certificate contains 128 observations in every layout.','E068')
    M('Shared evidence needs one column; the cyclic layout and all eight tested independent layouts need twelve', 'The minimum exact column certificate uses one column under shared support, versus twelve in the cyclic and all eight tested independent layouts','E069')
    A(r"The subsequent controls report selected coverage relative to each control's own baseline, separately from preference precision, across all nominal selection fractions and pooling rules.",r'The subsequent controls use each control\textquotesingle s own baseline for selected coverage. Their lists can differ, so these values are not retention gains on an identical output set; preference precision is separate.','E088')
    A(r"The returned annotated subset's MQM mean is compared with the $K_{\rm lab}$ highest-consensus annotated test outputs, using the original label-blind tie key.",r'We compare the returned annotated subset\textquotesingle s mean MQM with the mean for the $K_{\rm lab}$ highest-consensus outputs among all annotated test outputs, using the original label-blind tie key.','E091')
    A('Each order is reused across budgets, with separate first positive-gap and exact stopping states for each budget.', 'For each budget, we locate its first positive-gap and exact stopping prefixes on the same budget-independent acquisition path.','E094')
    A('Complete CSV/JSON results also retain all four acquisition strategies, full-information baseline, quality diagnostic, exact stop, witness decomposition and per-replacement loss.',r'Complete result paths and field meanings for acquisition orders, masks, stopping targets, quality diagnostics, witness decompositions and replacement-specific losses are listed in \nolinkurl{RESULT_DATA_DICTIONARY.md}. The prepared code bundle includes the listed summary artifacts; full third-party matrices and raw NLP traces remain outside that bundle.','E097,I005')
    A('The second term divides retained noninvariant outputs by all baseline-selected outputs, not by the noninvariant subset.',r'Both terms divide by $|S_0|$. The second is the selected-set share retained because its worst-case cost fits the budget, not retention within the noninvariant subset.','E098')
    A("The analysis uses the archive's WMT24 release files despite the updated host.", 'The analysis uses the WMT24 files inside that archive; the wmt26 hosting path does not define the evaluation year.','E099')
    # This sentence may already be fully precise; preserve its established label scope.
    A('They remain probes: no performance-based evaluator removal, cutoff refit or candidate-family change follows.', 'These streams are probes; their diagnostic performance does not trigger evaluator removal, cutoff refitting or candidate-family changes.','E103')
    A(r'\texttt{review-revision/wmt23-official/source-manifest.json}',r'\nolinkurl{review-revision/acceptance-review-implementation/wmt23-official-files.json}','E090')
    # Paths need line breaking in two columns; no anonymous identity is inserted.
    a=re.sub(r'\\texttt\{([^{}]*[/][^{}]*)\}',r'\\nolinkurl{\1}',a)
    for n,t in [('main.tex',m),('appendix.tex',a)]: (ROOT/'manuscript'/n).write_text(t)
    existing=json.loads((OUT/'edit-log.json').read_text());(OUT/'edit-log.json').write_text(json.dumps(existing+log,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\n')
    print(json.dumps({'additional_operations':len(log)}))
if __name__=='__main__':main()
